# What must never enter the build context.
#
# Two jobs: keep the image small, and make it impossible for a local secret or a
# local database to be copied into a layer by accident. Anything listed here is
# invisible to COPY, so it cannot ship even if a Dockerfile line is careless.

# ---- Secrets: never in an image ----
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/appsettings.Development.json
**/appsettings.Local.json
**/secrets.json
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx

# ---- Local databases: the image must start with an empty volume ----
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
backend/Data/uploads/

# ---- Build output and dependencies (rebuilt inside the image) ----
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
**/.vs/
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/

# ---- VCS and tooling ----
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.dockerignore
**/.DS_Store

# ---- Docs and local-only files ----
*.md
!DEPLOY.md
docker-compose*.yml
Dockerfile
